# Implementation Plan - Specific Business Model Playbooks

# Goal Description
Refine the copywriting playbooks to be strictly tailored to the **"Fully Managed Automation Service"** business model described in [reference/01.mdx](file:///u:/automation/template/reference/01.mdx).
The templates must explicitly force the writer to answer the specific buyer questions from [reference/03.mdx](file:///u:/automation/template/reference/03.mdx) using the "We handle everything" value proposition.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Business Model Integration**: The playbooks will no longer be generic. They will specifically instruct the user to write about "Managed Automation", "No technical skills needed", and "Hosted on our servers", as per `reference/01`.
> **FAQ Requirement**: Every relevant template will now include an FAQ section at the end.

## Proposed Changes

I will update the files in `u:\automation\template\playbook`.

### Core Strategy: The "Answer The Question" Format
Each section in the playbook will now look like this:
1.  **The Buyer Question**: (From `reference/03`) e.g., *"Do I get it right away or do I have to think too hard?"*
2.  **The Business Answer**: (From `reference/01`) e.g., *"We automate it end-to-end. You just tell us the process."*
3.  **The Framework**: How to write this answer.

### Playbook Updates

